    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d249">

                <pb facs="0273" n="157" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg157"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 893.77/1229.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Minister to the
                            Secretary of State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Peking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-10-05T15:00:00+08:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 5, 1912—3 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>On September 30 the Belgian company that constructed railway Kaifeng to Honan
                    signed a new contract to build line from Haichou via Kaifeng to Lanchou, in
                    Kansuh, for 215,000,000 francs, the railway to be security. When contract
                    ratified, 5,000,000 taels will be paid China, nominally to purchase line already
                    constructed.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Calhoun.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
